  <h1>Smart Room Monitor and Bus Collision Solver</h1>
  <p><strong>Technology:</strong> I2C</p>

  <h2>Parts Used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>ESP32</li>
    <li>SSD1306 OLED (0x3C)</li>
    <li>MPU6050 Accelerometer/Gyro (0x69 via ADO pin)</li>
    <li>DS1307 RTC (0x68)</li>
    <li>I2C LCD1602 (0x27)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How It Uses I2C to Its Full Extent</h2>
  <p>
    This project uses only I2C to connect multiple devices on two wires while avoiding address conflicts.
    It scans the bus at startup, resolves the 0x68 address clash between the DS1307 RTC and MPU6050 by
    using 0x69 for the MPU6050, and updates a live tilt graph on the OLED and time on the LCD.
  </p>

